From: J716s bringup
Subject: [PATCH] Permit unencrypted volumes when the hardware keybag is unavailable

Base: sgan81/apfs-fuse 66b86bd525e8cb90f9012543be89b1f092b75cf3.
Apple Silicon seals the keybag to hardware; System and Preboot need no key.
Do not mislabel the container as unencrypted: ApfsVolume::Init still requires
GetVolumeKey for encrypted volumes. DeviceLinux opens the source O_RDONLY.
Include the integer header explicitly for GCC 16.

--- a/ApfsLib/ApfsContainer.cpp
+++ b/ApfsLib/ApfsContainer.cpp
@@ -186,8 +186,9 @@
 	{
 		if (!m_keymgr.Init(m_nx.nx_keylocker.pr_start_addr, m_nx.nx_keylocker.pr_block_count, m_nx.nx_uuid))
 		{
-			std::cerr << "Initialization of KeyManager failed." << std::endl;
-			return false;
+			// Apple Silicon seals the container keybag to hardware. Unencrypted
+			// volumes need no key; encrypted volumes still require GetVolumeKey.
+			std::cerr << "KeyManager unavailable; only unencrypted volumes can be read." << std::endl;
 		}
 	}
 
--- a/ApfsLib/PList.h
+++ b/ApfsLib/PList.h
@@ -1,5 +1,6 @@
 #pragma once
 
+#include <cstdint>
 #include <vector>
 #include <map>
 #include <memory>
